# Dire Downdraft ({3}{U}, instant) costs {1} less if it targets an attacking or tapped creature (CR 601.2f, 118.7a). Bot2's
# Action News Crew has vigilance, so when it attacks it stays untapped: only "attacking" applies. On turn 3 it is neither
# attacking nor tapped and Bot1's three Moxen are short of {3}{U}; on turn 4 the same three pay exactly {2}{U}. Its owner Bot2
# accepts the top of its library, so the Crew is drawn again, and it deals no damage.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Dire Downdraft
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Action News Crew
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Action News Crew.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Hand.Dire Downdraft.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Action News Crew; Mana: short)
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Action News Crew > Bot1)
? Bot2.Battlefield.Action News Crew.Tapped = false
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dire Downdraft.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Action News Crew)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Accept

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 2
Bot2.Library.Top = Action News Crew
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Dire Downdraft
